<td id="A6.T9.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 4.30554pt;">
<span id="A6.T9.6.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A6.T9.6.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Conv2d: 256 <math id="A6.T9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 256 (3×3, stride=1, pad=1, no bias) <math id="A6.T9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> BatchNorm2d (256, momentum=0.9) <math id="A6.T9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> ReLU <math id="A6.T9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> MaxPool2d (2×2, stride=2).</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T9.6.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T9.6.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-bottom: 4.30554pt;"><span id="A6.T9.6.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Residual Block</span></th>
<td id="A6.T9.6.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: 4.30554pt;">
<span id="A6.T9.6.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A6.T9.6.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">(256 channels) Two 3×3 Conv2d layers with BatchNorm2d (momentum=0.9) and ReLU, connected by a skip connection.</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T9.6.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T9.6.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="A6.T9.6.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Final Layers</span></th>
<td id="A6.T9.6.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb">
<span id="A6.T9.6.8.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:284.5pt;">
<span id="A6.T9.6.8.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">ReLU <math id="A6.T9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> MaxPool2d (2×2, stride=2) <math id="A6.T9.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> Flatten <math id="A6.T9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> FC1: 1024 <math id="A6.T9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 128 (ReLU) <math id="A6.T9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> FC2: 128 <math id="A6.T9.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 64 (ReLU) <math id="A6.T9.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> FC3: 64 <math id="A6.T9.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> 10.</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Vision transformer (ViT)</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The ViT-Base/Patch-16/224 vision transformer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> first tokenized 224 x 224 RGB images into non-overlapping 16 x 16 patches, projects them linearly into a <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=768" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>768</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=768</annotation></semantics></math> dimensional embedding via a Conv2d patch-embedding layer that then appends learnable positional embeddings.
A sequence of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=12</annotation></semantics></math> encoder blocks process these <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{patches}}=(224/16)^{2}=196" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>patches</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>196</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{patches}}=(224/16)^{2}=196</annotation></semantics></math> tokens.
Each block consists of a LayerNorm, multi-head self-attention (with 12 heads, each of 64 dimensions, implemented with a <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3d\to 3d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3d\to 3d</annotation></semantics></math> Query-Key-Value linear layer and output projection, residual connections, followed by a two-layer MLP of width <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4d=3{,}072" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3,072</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4d=3{,}072</annotation></semantics></math> with GELU activation and dropout.
After the final block, a global classification token’s representation is layer-normalized and fed through a linear head to produce 1,000 ImageNet logits.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The ViT-Base model achieves 93% top-1 training accuracy and 85% top-1 validation accuracy.
The extracted activations from the four chosen layers each have dimension <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\ell}\in\{768,768,768,1{,}000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>768,768,768</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>000</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\ell}\in\{768,768,768,1{,}000\}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
We use <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> validation set samples and a uniform random sampling of 100 training samples from each class of the <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> classes, resulting in a total of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> samples for clustering each layer’s activations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Computational details</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments were carried out on a single MacBook Pro equipped with an Apple M2 Max chip and 32 GB of RAM, running macOS and Python 3.10 with PyTorch 2.6.0. We instantiated the pretrained VisionTransformer via “model = timm.create<math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\_" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>_</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\_</annotation></semantics></math>model(‘vit<math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\_" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>_</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\_</annotation></semantics></math>base<math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\_" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>_</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\_</annotation></semantics></math>patch16<math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\_" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>_</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\_</annotation></semantics></math>224’, pretrained=True)” (timm package version 1.0.15).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Clustering is sufficiently fast for practitioners as the CelebA forward pass for <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> samples takes <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;20</annotation></semantics></math> seconds and clustering takes <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;30</annotation></semantics></math> seconds.
At scale, bottlenecks of cluster paths include forward passes to store activations at each layer of interest.
The ViT forward pass for <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> ImageNet samples (224x224x3 RGB images) took approximately under 1.5 hours and clustering takes <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;2</annotation></semantics></math> minutes.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Asset sources and licensing</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CIFAR-10: We use the CIFAR-10 dataset from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite>, distributed under the MIT license (<a href="https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.cs.toronto.edu/~kriz/cifar.html</a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CelebA: We use the CelebA face-attribute dataset (Liu et al., 2015), “CelebA Research-Only License (MMLAB)” for non-commercial research (<a href="https://mmlab.ie.cuhk.edu.hk/projects/CelebA.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://mmlab.ie.cuhk.edu.hk/projects/CelebA.html</a> and <a href="https://datasetninja.com/celeb-faces-attributes" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://datasetninja.com/celeb-faces-attributes</a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ImageNet: Our ViT experiments use the ILSVRC2012 subset of ImageNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">45</a>]</cite>, which is “available for free to researchers for non-commercial use” (<a href="https://image-net.org/index.php" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://image-net.org/index.php</a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ViT checkpoint: We load a publicly released ViT-Base/patch-16/224 model checkpoint from the official repository, distributed under the Apache 2.0 license(<a href="https://github.com/rwightman/pytorch-image-models/blob/master/LICENSE" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/rwightman/pytorch-image-models/blob/master/LICENSE</a>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A8.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A8.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">PyTorch: All training and evaluation code is built on PyTorch (BSD 3-Clause License - <a href="https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/LICENSE" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/main/LICENSE</a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
</article>
